# Research — Dry-Run Apply Reuse

## Executive Summary

Objective: identify the narrowest additive seam for attaching an opaque apply affordance to every successful mutating manage_docs(dry_run=True) response. Confidence: high for source mappings; low for remote/PR state because governed shell inspection was denied while this worker lacked a resolver-verified claim.

The narrowest seam is the shared post-router response finalization in src/scribe_mcp/doc_management/runtime.py:3190-3224. It receives every handler response, action, dry_run, active project, execution context, and normalized scope, and already performs common enrichment. Add one helper there, gated by response.ok and dry_run and _is_manage_docs_write_intent(action), to attach a compact receipt. Create has an early return at runtime.py:3094-3100, so invoke the same helper there too.

## System Surface Map

1. Successful mutating dry-run response → runtime.py:3190-3224 → MCP return. Confidence: high. Trace: tools/manage_docs.py:271-340 → runtime router runtime.py:3102-3180 → finalizer runtime.py:3190-3224 → host result. UI is intentionally absent per SPEC.
2. Action authority/classification → runtime.py:39-142 and 145-166; write-intent predicate 281-282. Confidence: high. Trace: host schema tools/manage_docs.py:65-126 → live build_manage_docs_action_manifest → VALID_ACTIONS/ACTION_ROUTER → mutation predicate.
3. Mutation execution/preimage → manager.py:154-169, 197-231, 1332-1375. Confidence: high. Trace: actions/edit.py:131-164 → injected apply_doc_change runtime.py:3128 → manager lock/CAS → actions/edit.py:460-487 response.

## Core System Seams

Shared finalization runtime.py:3190-3224 copies anchor fields, adds project context, case binding, warnings, and returns. Receipt attachment belongs after successful response enrichment and before return. Confidence: high.

Create special handling runtime.py:3094-3100 returns early; a helper only in the normal finalizer would omit create. Call the helper before both return sites. Confidence: high.

Host schema tools/manage_docs.py:65-126 derives action enum from build_manage_docs_action_manifest()[all_actions] at 86-100; response adds supported manifest at 321-322. A new action needs runtime authority/router plus live enum; no prompt, roster, or skill edit. Confidence: high.

Mutation actions runtime.py:154-166 are replace_section, apply_patch, replace_range, append, status_update, frontmatter_update, normalize_headers, generate_toc, replace_text, validate_crosslinks, metadata_repair. Create and rehome_doc are additionally writes via runtime.py:281-282. Read-only registration actions are list_sections, list_checklist_items, preview_reconciliation, search at 179-184; quality/scaffold and query paths are not mutation actions. Confidence: high.

## Invariants

Session/project identity: context preparation requires a project at runtime.py:2611-2642; unsafe fallback resolution is rejected for writes at 2780-2798. Confidence: high.

Path authorization: non-dry-run write intent invokes assert_writes_allowed at runtime.py:2697-2702. Confidence: high.

CAS/hash/locking: DocChangeResult before_hash/after_hash at manager.py:154-169; ANCHOR_DIGEST_ALGORITHM at 197; cross-process lock at 200-231; patch_source_hash and expected_anchor_sha256 flow through 1332-1375. Confidence: high.

Audit: manager.py:61-101 has operation logging; handlers receive append_entry. Receipt issue/consume should append linked preview/apply events with opaque ID only. Confidence: high.

TTL/idempotency gap: source search found agent_manager.py:53-101,279-282 15-minute session lease, but no receipt-specific persistent consumed-token store. A process-local dict is unsafe across workers/restarts. Confidence: medium/high. Receipt repository/storage API is UNKNOWN and must be designed or verified.

Serialization: manage_docs.py:311-322 returns JSON-safe payloads and live supported action metadata; mcp_adapter.py:182-296 normalizes/validates tool definitions. Confidence: high.

## Risk Surfaces

Create omission if only normal finalizer changes (high). Receipt must not expose secrets or internal session/project state (high). Hash-only capture may be insufficient for create/rehome resolution (medium). Multi-process persistence and atomic single-consume semantics are unverified (high). Existing edit dry-run shape at actions/edit.py:460-476 includes dry_run, preview_only, write_applied, diff, hashes; preserve all additively (high).

## Existing Verification Surfaces

Representative tests: tests/test_manage_docs_runtime_action_classification.py; test_manage_docs_anchor_cas.py; test_gen_001_baseline_hash_recorded.py; test_manage_docs_actor_identity.py; test_manage_docs_session_binding.py; test_project_identity_preflight.py; test_manage_docs_create_doc.py; test_manage_docs_patch_range.py; test_manage_docs_frontmatter_contract.py; test_manage_docs_generate_toc.py; test_manage_docs_schema_keystone.py; test_mcp_adapter.py; test_response_formatter_helpers.py; test_manage_docs_quality_check.py.

New tests must cover create/edit/rehome successful previews, read-only and quality no-affordance, apply-once, deterministic replay, expiry, wrong actor/session/project, preimage drift, invalid receipt, and host-valid MCP result content. Full suite is out of scope.

