## Recommendations

Prefer one new server-issued receipt/apply action over overloading an existing edit action. Keep automatic affordance generation in the shared finalizer and create twin. Additive object recommendation: apply_receipt with opaque id, action, expires_at, preimage_sha256, and apply_action; do not expose normalized payload. Follow-up accepts receipt ID plus actor/session context, reloads normalized operation, then rechecks policy/path/preimage and atomically consumes once. Reuse an existing project storage only if it proves atomic CAS/expiry; otherwise add a narrowly scoped repository. Exact invocation field and persistence schema are UNKNOWN pending Blueprint design.

## Handoff

Blueprint should design around the shared post-handler finalizer plus create early-return twin, preserve the action manifest and mutation predicate, preserve session-bound project/path policy and manager CAS/lock/hash invariants, and verify representative mutation/read-only and receipt lifecycle tests.

## MCP SDK v2 and Branch Truth

NOT VERIFIED / BLOCKED. Governed read-only Git/remote inspection was denied with WORK_ITEM_MUTATION_DENIED[BIND_MISSING], and claim_work_item separately returned SEAT_PROOF_MALFORMED. No claim is made about MCP SDK v2 on main, migration branches/worktrees, remotes, or PRs. Orchestrator must run the prescribed read-only command set from a verified bound seat.

## Unknowns

Receipt persistence schema/API, atomic consume and cleanup; exact new action invocation; whether create/rehome retain sufficient canonical operation data; current remote/PR state. No RI query was used, so no RI honesty envelope applies.

## Self-QA

PASS for source-grounded mapping, confidence labels, explicit unknowns, tests, and handoff. NOT READY for complete package handoff until verified v2 branch facts and bind evidence are supplied.
